From ebf353634293cde65b84cb1d582a152959674e3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:54:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Learner: hardcoded max rpm and linear forces as profile
 settings

Replace the build flags LEARNER_HARDCODE_MAXRPM and
LEARNER_HARDCODE_LINEAR_FORCES with settings:

- learner_hardcode_max_rpm (0..200000, default 0)
  0: max rpm from the learned motor model
  otherwise: use this max rpm for all motors (flag used 37000)

- learner_hardcode_g1_fz (-32000..32000, default 0)
  0: learned fx, fy, fz
  otherwise: fx = fy = 0, fz = this value, same units as
  indi_act_g1_fz (flag used -438)

The HexDemo_post_fix profiles drop the two #defines and set 37000 and
-438 instead, so those builds behave as before. learnerConfig PG
version 2 -> 3. Both settings are written to the blackbox header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ShSV4NN8hhaJjwwPzXK1XY
